# Python virtual environment. About 1.3 GB of installable packages - anyone
# cloning this rebuilds it from server/requirements.txt in a few minutes.
server/.venv/
.venv/

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Working backups written while editing. The history in git replaces these.
*.bak-*
*.orig-backup

# Hero clips, if they are ever added. Large binaries do not belong in git.
site/assets/*.mp4
site/assets/*.webm

# The "try a sample clip" strip, built by scripts/make_samples.py from clips
# you already hold. The manifest is ignored along with the videos on purpose:
# committing samples.json without the clips it names would give a fresh clone
# a row of buttons that all fail to load.
site/assets/samples/

# Fine-tuned weights written by finetune_clips.py. ~340 MB of safetensors, which
# does not belong in git. It IS needed to build the container image, so keep a
# copy (Drive, a release asset) and place it at
# deploy/container/ctf_pretrained/vit_finetuned/ before building. Without it the
# image falls back to the stock hub weights, which score at chance.
vit_finetuned/

# Test footage. Celeb-DF and FaceForensics++ are licensed for research use and
# must NOT be redistributed - committing a clip here would breach the agreement
# signed to obtain the dataset, quite apart from the repository size.
*.mp4
*.mov
*.webm
*.mkv
*.avi
*.m4v

# Local scratch
*.log
.claude/settings.local.json

# OS noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Evaluation working files under reports/ -- per-frame probability caches,
# extracted crops, reliability and confusion plots. All regenerated by re-running
# the script that wrote them. The small JSON summaries beside them ARE committed:
# they are the measurements STATUS.md quotes, and a table without its source
# number is the thing this project keeps having to go back and re-derive.
reports/*_cache/
reports/*.png

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The two front-page clips are the ONE exception to the blanket video rule
# above. They are the project owner's own footage, cleared for publication, and
# the site is deployed from this repository - so if they are not committed the
# public front page falls back to empty placeholder panels.
#
# These negations sit at the end of the file on purpose: a later pattern wins,
# so they have to come after both `site/assets/*.mp4` and the blanket `*.mp4`.
#
# Nothing else may be added here. The sample-strip clips are Celeb-DF and
# FaceForensics++ footage, licensed for research use only; publishing them to a
# public URL would breach the agreement signed to obtain the datasets.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!site/assets/reel.mp4
!site/assets/real.mp4
!deploy/container/site/assets/reel.mp4
!deploy/container/site/assets/real.mp4

# The published demo pair behind the deployed site's sample strip: one deepfake
# the detector flags at 0.9405, and its genuine counterpart. Cleared for
# publication by the project owner. Same reasoning as the hero clips - the site
# is deployed from this repository, so a clip that is not committed does not
# exist for any visitor.
#
# site/assets/samples/ stays ignored in full and must never be added here: that
# folder is built from Celeb-DF footage, which is licensed for research use only.
!site/assets/demo/*.mp4
!site/assets/demo/samples.json
!deploy/container/site/assets/demo/*.mp4
!deploy/container/site/assets/demo/samples.json
